      "text": "57-year-old female presenting with chest pain for 7 hours. Character: pressure like a heavy weight; radiation: to the jaw; aggravated by walking or climbing stairs; relieved by nothing. Severity 7/10. Associated: breathlessness, nausea. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 3 years; Coronary artery disease, stent 6 years ago; Appendectomy in 2021. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Aspirin 75 mg; Atorvastatin 20 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: diabetes. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: EMERGENCY."
